1. First disconnection uses a TBS protection strategy to protect the alcohols
2. The conjugated diene is formed using a Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons reaction
3. The aldehyde precursor is formed by DIBAL-H reduction of the ester
4. The ester is formed by nucleophilic substitution of a bromide
5. The starting materials are all commercially available compounds

Each step is supported by the templates found in the database and follows the reaction types mentioned in the hints. The route has more than 5 reactions when including the protection/deprotection steps, and leads to commercially available starting materials.
